# Frozen-integrity depends on the checkout reproducing the committed bytes.
#
# `scripts/check_surfaced.py` transitively imports `experimentL/harness/
# execute_recipe.py` -> `experimentJ/harness/macro_v2.py`, whose import-time
# `verify_v1_source()` hashes `experimentI/harness/gate_I.py` byte-exactly
# against a hash frozen in `experimentJ/expected.json`. Every file in that chain
# is frozen evidence or a historical harness, so none of them may be edited --
# which leaves the bytes on disk as the only free variable. A CRLF checkout
# makes that guard report VOID on an artifact that never changed.
#
# Every committed blob in this repository is already LF (measured: 0 of 76
# frozen artifacts have CRLF in their blob), so this file changes no committed
# content. It makes a checkout faithful to what was committed.
#
# See issue #7 and docs/development/initiatives.md I-7.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts keep exact-byte identity and are never EOL-translated.
# The frozen estate's 38 binary artifacts are all xlsx.
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.pyc  binary
